      "description": "Khaba Fort, overlooking the abandoned village of Khabha near Jaisalmer, Rajasthan, stands amidst the stark landscape of the Thar Desert. Built from locally available golden-yellow sandstone, the fort is characterized by its long defensive walls, crenellated parapets, projecting bastions and a prominent arched entrance. I have framed the monument with the winding road leading towards the central gateway, emphasizing the fort's imposing horizontal form, its isolation and its close relationship with the surrounding desert landscape.",
